---
import Flower from '../components/decor/Flower.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="About Lin Bele Jacobsen, senior UX designer and product owner."
>
  <main id="main" class="page-main">
    <div class="page-grid about-page">
      <div class="page-grid__reading about__copy">
        <p class="kicker">About</p>
        <div class="about__title-row">
          <div class="about__decor" aria-hidden="true">
            <Flower name="cosmos" />
          </div>
          <h1>Me until now</h1>
        </div>
        <p>
          I love looking for ways to automate and simplify mundane boring chores, giving room for more rewarding tasks. My biggest passion is designing for users at work.
        </p>
        <p>
          I am a senior UX/UI designer based in Norway, currently looking for a new position where I can create value.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="page-grid about-more">
      <div class="page-grid__reading prose">
        <h2>Roles and methodology</h2>
        <div class="fact-groups">
          <div>
            <h3>Roles</h3>
            <ul class="roles-list">
              <li>UI Designer</li>
              <li>UX Designer</li>
              <li>Agile Product Owner</li>
              <li>Scrum Master</li>
              <li>Web analyst</li>
              <li>Agile Coach</li>
              <li>Accessibility expert</li>
              <li>Developer (outdated)</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
        <h3>Passions</h3>
        <p>
          Learning new skills, user research, Agile, Figma design systems, accessibility, redesigning data heavy
          complex tools, asynchronous work methods, travel and culture.
        </p>

        <h2>Work</h2>
        <p>
          I work for Vokser, a small but valuable company in Norway. I work as a UX lead - consultant — my clients
          are mostly Norwegian and I do what I have done for the past 25 years. Designing easy-to-use digital tools
          that make people's workday more efficient!
        </p>

        <h2>Design philosophy</h2>
        <p>
          When designing I will focus on creating simple, efficient and beautiful experiences that can be used by
          all users. Reducing cognitive load wherever I can! After doing user testing for many years, I've met
          users with sight and hearing disabilities, broken arms - young children, elderly and all in between. I
          have also designed for senior experts working alongside newly hired juniors. I want to design and write
          copy that is intuitive and easy to use for all of them!
        </p>

        <h2>Research repository</h2>
        <p>
          To keep things interesting I am adding new skills, currently focusing on building a system for storing
          user research. Doing user research is expensive, often they sit vacant in a folder somewhere. Findings
          are reusable across projects and products so it makes sense to preserve it and make it reusable! I am
          also trying out AI to be able to find and combine user insights.
        </p>

        <h2>Mentor</h2>
        <p>
          Every week, during evenings I also volunteer as a mentor for UX Designers and Product managers. Helping
          young designers find their footing and build an exciting career short- and long-term.
        </p>
        <p>
          I've also done some local events - Figma Fridays - helping young designers be more collaborative and
          efficient in Figma.
        </p>

        <figure>
          <img
            src="/assets/about/portrait.png"
            alt="A woman in profile with her eyes closed, leaning against a tree trunk in a forest at golden hour, wearing a yellow jumper and a plaid scarf."
            width="1920"
            height="1272"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
          />
        </figure>

        <h2>Personal</h2>
        <p>
          I probably have more hobbies than other people have socks. I love the ocean -&gt; Surfing, diving, open
          water swimming, paddle boarding, and sailing. I do figure skating and free-heel skiing in winter. I have
          a dog and love hiking forests, the countryside and mountains. I play the flute and love classical music.
          Travelling has been a big part of my life, and Asia is always my first choice. During my summers I go
          south to the French west coast for surfing.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-page {
    row-gap: var(--space-4);
  }

  .about__title-row {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: flex-end;
    column-gap: 1.25rem;
    row-gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .about__decor {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    height: clamp(6rem, 13vw, 9rem);
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  @media (max-width: 767px) {
    .about__decor {
      height: clamp(4.5rem, 20vw, 6rem);
    }
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--step-3);
    font-weight: 300;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    line-height: 1.15;
  }

  .about__copy p {
    max-width: var(--reading-max);
  }

  .about-more {
    margin-top: var(--space-5);
  }

  /*
   * .prose h2 always carries its own 2.2em margin-top for section breaks
   * further down the article. Here it's the first child, so that margin
   * doesn't collapse away into .about-more's own margin-top (grid items
   * are a margin-collapsing boundary) — it stacks on top of it instead,
   * roughly doubling the gap above "Roles and methodology" compared to
   * every other h2 break in this article. Zeroing it leaves .about-more's
   * margin-top as the section's only separator.
   */
  .about-more .prose > h2:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .fact-groups {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }

  .fact-groups h3,
  .prose h3 + p {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .fact-groups ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.2em;
  }

  .roles-list {
    columns: 2;
    column-gap: var(--space-4);
    max-width: 26rem;
  }

  .roles-list li {
    break-inside: avoid;
  }
</style>
